An on-screen list of the pad controls

Craft is a keyboard and mouse game and says nowhere what its keys are: it
expects a player who has read the README. On a console there is no README and
no keyboard, so the mapping in `shim/glfw_shim.c` is the only description of
how to play, and it is not on screen.

This draws the pad's mapping in the bottom right, through Craft's own
`render_text` and the font it already loads, so it costs one more text pass and
no new asset. It reads the same way the HUD does and sits opposite it.

The lines name pad buttons rather than the keys they produce, because the key is
an implementation detail of the shim: Square and Circle arrive as mouse buttons,
and L1 and R1 as `CRAFT_KEY_ITEM_PREV` and `CRAFT_KEY_ITEM_NEXT`. Jump is listed
because nothing else says it exists.

The list is every control a pad has, and that is all of them. Chat, commands and
signs need a keyboard: they open a typing line that `main.c` leaves only on
Enter or Escape, which a pad cannot produce. There is no entry for a pause menu
because Craft has none.

The array is `char *const` and not `const char *`, because upstream's
`render_text` takes a non-const `char *`.

`SHOW_CONTROLS_TEXT` defaults to 0 and is wrapped in `#ifndef`, so this changes
nothing for a desktop build and the port turns it on with
`-DSHOW_CONTROLS_TEXT=1`. Made overridable rather than changed, as patch 0001
is, so the file stays close to upstream and the next rebase is a smaller job.

--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -33,6 +33,9 @@
 #define SHOW_INFO_TEXT 1
 #define SHOW_CHAT_TEXT 1
 #define SHOW_PLAYER_NAMES 1
+#ifndef SHOW_CONTROLS_TEXT
+#define SHOW_CONTROLS_TEXT 0
+#endif
 
 // key bindings
 #define CRAFT_KEY_FORWARD 'W'
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -2885,6 +2885,23 @@
                 render_text(&text_attrib, ALIGN_LEFT, tx, ty, ts, text_buffer);
                 ty -= ts * 2;
             }
+            if (SHOW_CONTROLS_TEXT) {
+                static char *const controls[] = {
+                    "left stick - move",
+                    "right stick - look",
+                    "square - break",
+                    "circle - place",
+                    "L1 / R1 - block",
+                    "cross - jump",
+                };
+                int count = sizeof(controls) / sizeof(controls[0]);
+                float cx = g->width - ts / 2;
+                float cy = ts / 2 + ts * 2 * (count - 1);
+                for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+                    render_text(&text_attrib, ALIGN_RIGHT, cx, cy, ts, controls[i]);
+                    cy -= ts * 2;
+                }
+            }
             if (SHOW_PLAYER_NAMES) {
                 if (player != me) {
                     render_text(&text_attrib, ALIGN_CENTER,
